 HISTORY                                                            43 1451
 -------                                                            43 1451
 This library was produced by the Low Energy Interaction Physics    43 1451
 (LEIP) group at North Carolina State University, USA. The          43 1451
 inelastic scattering cross section libraries for Si in 3C-SiC      43 1451
 were fully developed using ab-initio lattice dynamics (AILD)       43 1451
 methods [1]. The phonon DOS used in this evaluation was            43 1451
 generated using an AILD model for 3C-SiC [2]. The trigonal         43 1451
 structure, belonging to the F-43m space group (#216), was          43 1451
 modeled in VASP [3-5] using the GGA exchange-correlation           43 1451
 functional with a 900eV plane-wave cutoff energy and a 3x3x3       43 1451
 Monkhorst-Pack k-mesh. The phonon density of states was            43 1451
 generated using a 3x3x3 supercell in PHONON [6] via the            43 1451
 dynamical matrix method. For this evaluation, the energy grid      43 1451
 resolution was increased in the PHONON DOS evaluation. Nine        43 1451
 temperatures are available in this library. The Full Law           43 1451
 Analysis Scattering System Hub (FLASSH) was used to produce MT     43 1451
 = 2 (coherent) and MT = 4 data [7]. By convention, MAT=43 and      43 1451
 ZA=143 are used for Si in 3C-SiC.                                  43 1451
                                                                    43 1451
 The silicon carbide evluation improved the ENDF/B-VIII.0           43 1451
 evaluation with key updates: (1) lattice constants from            43 1451
 experimental values were used [8], (2) the DOS was improved        43 1451
 with increased resolution, and (3) the coherent elastic was        43 1451
 updated to the cubic evaluation in FLASSH [7].                     43 1451
